// SwWeb migrate: default mapping of the legacy front end globals (old common/common.js, app/application.js) to the new Sw API.
// Built from the old common.js / application.js globals and their Sw counterparts (core/README.md, ui/README.md and PORTING.md part A in SysWeaver.HttpServer/srcWeb). See the SwWeb README ("migrate", "Mapping file").
//
// Entry forms (in "Globals", and in "Members" of an object entry):
//   "old": "Sw.New.Path"                                 Rename (same arguments and semantics), every use as a global.
//   "old": { "New": "...", "MaxArgs": 2, "Note": "" }      Rename calls with at most MaxArgs arguments, report the others.
//   "old": { "New": "...", "Positional": 1, "Options": ["A", "B"] }  old(x, y, z) -> New(x, { A: y, B: z }); more arguments are reported.
//   "old": { "Kind": "Property", "New": "..." }            old() (no arguments) becomes the property New; other uses are reported.
//   "old": { "Kind": "Report", "Suggest": "...", "Note": "" } Never rewritten, every use is reported with the suggestion.
//   "old": { "Kind": "Ignore" }                            Not a legacy name (no rewrite, no report).
//   "old": { "Members": { "member": <entry> }, "New": "..." } An object: "old.member" is mapped per member; unmapped members use New + ".member"
//                                                          when New is set, else they are reported. A bare "old" uses New (or is reported).
//   "Shell": true marks a shell feature (a page using it loads sw/shell.js + sw/shell.css).
// "Css": selector hooks in .css files and <style> elements: ".OldClass" / "OldElement" -> new selector text. Rewritten only with "Safe": true.
// "Library": "<file>" on a section: its names are legacy aliases that this library still provides; uses that can't be renamed are reported
//   but don't need sw/compat.js. Only pure renames (same object / function) are "New" strings, wrappers with other arguments are "Report".
// "Tokens": css custom properties (design tokens): "--old": { "New": "--new", "Safe": true } renames every var(--old) use (css, style
//   attributes, JavaScript strings) because --old is an alias of --new (identical value); entries without "Safe" are reported by the Design v2
//   rules (check --design, migrate --level design) with "New" as the suggestion. Definitions (--old: value) are never rewritten.
//   An option named "-" in "Options" drops that argument (the new API ignores it; only simple arguments such as literals are dropped).
// Sections can be added / extended by a --map file (same format; entries with the same name replace the default ones).
